2) Definitions & formulas (so we’re aligned)
- CAC (Customer Acquisition Cost) = Total Sales & Marketing spend in a period / Number of new customers acquired in that period.
- ARPU (Average Revenue Per User) = Revenue in period / Average number of active customers in that period (use monthly or annual basis consistently).
- Monthly churn rate (c) = proportion of customers lost each month.
- Customer lifetime (months) ≈ 1 / monthly churn (if churn is flat).
- Contribution margin per customer (monthly) = ARPU_monthly * Gross margin %.
- LTV (simple cohort approach) = ARPU_monthly * Gross margin % * (1 / monthly churn)
