2) Data I need to calculate accurate CAC and LTV
- Sales & Marketing spend (total) for the period you want to measure (last 12 months or last quarter)
- Number of new customers acquired in that same period
- Total active customers (or starting/ending cohorts)
- Average Revenue per User/account (ARPU) — monthly or annual
- Gross margin (contribution margin %) on revenue (or cost of goods sold)
- Customer churn (monthly or annual) or average customer lifetime
- Any segmentation you want (SMB vs Midmarket vs Enterprise) — if available

If you don’t have all of the above, I can run scenario/sensitivity tables using reasonable assumptions; below I explain the formulas, show examples, and give the finance narrative you can use.

Key formulas (simple, standard)
- CAC = Total Sales & Marketing spend (period) / # of New Customers acquired (same period)
- LTV (margin-based) = ARPU * Gross Margin % / Churn rate (if churn is monthly and ARPU is monthly)
  - Equivalently: LTV = Contribution margin per customer per month * Average lifetime (1 / monthly churn)
- CAC Payback (months) = CAC / (ARPU_month * Gross Margin)
- LTV : CAC target = at least 3 : 1 (good), payback typically < 12 months for growth-stage capital efficiency (benchmarks vary by business model)

Illustrative scenarios (using your reported revenue last quarter as a check)
- Monthly revenue = $3.2M / 3 = $1,066,667

Assumptions used for the examples below: S&M = 20% of revenue (you should replace with your actual S&M spend).

Scenario 1 — Low ARPU (volume, low touch)
- ARPU = $200 / month
- Gross margin = 65%
- Monthly churn = 5% (avg lifetime = 20 months)
- S&M (monthly) = 1,066,667 * 20% = $213,333
- New customers / month = 500 (assumption)
Calculations:
- CAC = 213,333 / 500 = $427
- LTV = 200 * 0.65 / 0.05 = $2,600
- LTV:CAC ≈ 6.1
- Payback = 427 / (200 * 0.65) ≈ 3.3 months

Scenario 2 — Mid ARPU (typical SaaS)
- ARPU = $1,000 / month
- Gross margin = 75%
- Monthly churn = 3% (avg lifetime ≈ 33.3 months)
- Same S&M monthly = $213,333
- New customers / month = 100
Calculations:
- CAC = 213,333 / 100 = $2,133
- LTV = 1,000 * 0.75 / 0.03 = $25,000
- LTV:CAC ≈ 11.7
- Payback = 2,133 / (1,000 * 0.75) ≈ 2.8 months

Scenario 3 — Enterprise (high ARPU, low volume)
- ARPU = $10,000 / month
- Gross margin = 80%
- Monthly churn = 1% (avg lifetime = 100 months)
- Same S&M monthly = $213,333
- New customers / month = 2
Calculations:
- CAC = 213,333 / 2 = $106,667
- LTV = 10,000 * 0.80 / 0.01 = $800,000
- LTV:CAC ≈ 7.5
- Payback = 106,667 / (10,000 * 0.8) ≈ 13.3 months

Notes on the examples
- These are illustrative — the LTV and CAC outcomes are extremely sensitive to churn, gross margin, ARPU, and how many customers you actually acquire for a given S&M spend.
