What I need from you to calculate real CAC & LTV
- Sales & marketing spend for the period you want to analyze (quarter or month). CAC should use the same period as new customers.  
- Number of new customers acquired during that period.  
- Total number of active customers (or ARPA / ARPU) so we can compute revenue per customer.  
- Gross margin (contribution margin %) on revenue.  
- Churn rate (monthly or annual) or average customer lifetime.  
If you don’t have churn, we can infer lifetime from retention or use scenario assumptions.

Formulas (simple, standard)
- CAC = (Sales & Marketing spend in period) / (New customers acquired in same period)  
- Monthly ARPU = (Revenue in period) / (Number of active customers in that period)  
- LTV (subscription-style) ≈ ARPU_month × Gross margin % × (1 / Monthly churn)  
  - or LTV = Lifetime revenue per customer × Gross margin %  
- LTV : CAC ratio = LTV / CAC  
- CAC payback (months) = CAC / (ARPU_month × Gross margin %)

Illustrative example (useful template you can plug numbers into)
- Revenue last quarter = $3.2M → monthly rev = $3.2M / 3 = $1,066,667  
- Assume (example) S&M last quarter = $480,000 and new customers last quarter = 40 → CAC = 480,000 / 40 = $12,000  
- Assume total active customers = 400 → ARPU_month = 1,066,667 / 400 ≈ $2,666.67  
- Assume gross margin = 70% and monthly churn = 2% → average lifetime ≈ 1 / 0.02 = 50 months  
- LTV ≈ 2,666.67 × 0.70 × 50 ≈ $93,333  
- LTV:CAC ≈ 93,333 / 12,000 ≈ 7.8 (very healthy)  
- CAC payback ≈ 12,000 / (2,666.67 × 0.70) ≈ 6.4 months (very quick)

