3) Formulas and metrics (clean, copyable)
- CAC = Total Sales & Marketing Spend (in period) / Number of New Customers Acquired (in same period)
- ARPU (monthly) = Total Monthly Revenue / Number of Active Customers
- For subscription businesses: LTV = (ARPU per month * Gross Margin %) / Monthly Churn Rate
  - Equivalently, LTV = ARPU * Gross Margin * Average Customer Lifetime (where Lifetime = 1 / churn)
- For non-subscription (transactional): LTV = Average Order Value * Purchase Frequency (per year) * Average Customer Lifetime (years) * Gross Margin
- LTV : CAC ratio = LTV / CAC (rule of thumb: target >= 3)
- CAC payback (months) = CAC / (Monthly gross margin per customer) where monthly gross margin per customer = ARPU * Gross Margin %

4) Worked examples (illustrative scenarios)
I’ll use your revenue last quarter = $3.2M → monthly revenue ≈ $1.067M. I’ll show three ARPU scenarios to demonstrate sensitivity. Assume gross margin = 70% (adjustable), and churn scenarios.

