- ARPU (monthly) = $10,000 → customers ≈ 1,066,667 / 10,000 ≈ 107 customers
- Monthly churn = 2% → Average lifetime = 50 months
- LTV = 10,000 * 0.70 / 0.02 = $350,000
- If S&M per quarter = $500k and new customers last quarter = 10 → CAC = $50k → LTV:CAC = 350k / 50k = 7x (excellent); payback = CAC / (ARPU*GM) = 50k / (7k) ≈ 7.1 months

Scenario B — Mid ARPU, moderate churn (mid-market SaaS)
- ARPU = $2,000/month → customers ≈ 533
- Monthly churn = 5% → Average lifetime = 20 months
- LTV = 2,000 * 0.70 / 0.05 = $28,000
- If S&M last quarter = $600k and new customers = 60 → CAC = $10k → LTV:CAC = 2.8x (close to target); payback = 10k / (1,400) ≈ 7.1 months

Scenario C — Low ARPU, higher churn (SMB/consumer)
- ARPU = $200/month → customers ≈ 5,333
- Monthly churn = 8% → Avg lifetime = 12.5 months
- LTV = 200 * 0.70 / 0.08 = $1,750
- If S&M last quarter = $400k and new customers = 1,000 → CAC = $400 → LTV:CAC = 4.4x (good); payback = 400 / (140) ≈ 2.9 months

